# /usr/share/lindos/tune/autostart-hide.list
# System-wide XDG autostart entries (/etc/xdg/autostart/<name>.desktop) that `lindos-tune apply`
# hides from XFCE sessions by adding `NotShowIn=XFCE;` (idempotent, marked with
# X-Lindos-Hidden=true so it can be reverted exactly).  Users can still start these apps from
# the menu; per-user overrides in ~/.config/autostart win over the system file.
#
# Syntax:  <desktop-basename> [if-disabled=<unit>]
#   if-disabled=<unit>  → hidden only while <unit> is disabled, un-hidden again when it is
#                         re-enabled (lindos-tune services enable <unit>).
#
# Deliberately NOT here: light-locker (screen lock), xfce4-power-manager, nm-applet, xfsettingsd,
# polkit agent, print-applet (small, useful), mintupdate (kept — the tray is what tells users
# about updates; it delays its own start), lindos-* entries.

# Mint's welcome screen is replaced by the Lindos OOBE (lindos-setup)
mintwelcome
# System-report tray (mintreport-tray) — run "System Reports" from the menu when needed
mintreport
# Ubuntu-style crash/telemetry helpers (no telemetry in Lindos)
apport
whoopsie
# Bluetooth tray only while the bluetooth service is disabled (Lite mode only — every other
# mode keeps bluetooth.service enabled by default, SPEC §8)
blueman-applet if-disabled=bluetooth.service
# Accessibility screen reader autostart (start it from Settings → Accessibility if needed)
orca-autostart
# Ubuntu report/onboard helpers not needed on XFCE
onboard-autostart
